  {"n": 1, "title": "Actions are by intentions", "narrator": "ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (1) and Muslim (1907)", "ar": "عَنْ أَمِيرِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَبِي حَفْصٍ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ يَقُولُ:  إنَّمَا الْأَعْمَالُ بِالنِّيَّاتِ، وَإِنَّمَا لِكُلِّ امْرِئٍ مَا نَوَى، فَمَنْ كَانَتْ هِجْرَتُهُ إلَى اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ فَهِجْرَتُهُ إلَى اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ، وَمَنْ كَانَتْ هِجْرَتُهُ لِدُنْيَا يُصِيبُهَا أَوْ امْرَأَةٍ يَنْكِحُهَا فَهِجْرَتُهُ إلَى مَا هَاجَرَ إلَيْهِ", "en": "I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Actions are only by intentions, and every person will have only what he intended. So whoever emigrated for Allah and His Messenger, his emigration is for Allah and His Messenger; and whoever emigrated for some worldly thing he wants to gain, or a woman he wants to marry, his emigration is for what he emigrated for.”", "lessons": ["Allah judges a deed by the intention behind it, so the same outward action can be worship or nothing at all.", "An intention lives in the heart. You do not need to say it aloud for it to count.", "Renew your intention before study, prayer and work, and check it again in the middle of a deed.", "Ordinary habits like eating, sleeping and working can earn reward when done with a good intention."], "quiz": [["According to this ḥadīth, what decides the value of an action?", "The intention behind it", "How many people see it", "How long it takes to do", "How difficult it feels"], ["The example the Prophet ﷺ gives in this ḥadīth is about:", "Emigration (hijrah)", "Fasting in Ramaḍān", "Giving charity in secret", "Praying at night"], ["Where does the intention (niyyah) live?", "In the heart", "On the tongue", "In the written word", "In the limbs"], ["Someone who emigrated to marry a woman receives:", "What he emigrated for", "The full reward of hijrah", "Half the reward of hijrah", "No result of any kind"], ["Which Companion narrated this ḥadīth?", "ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb", "Abū Hurayrah", "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās", "Anas ibn Mālik"]]},
  {"n": 2, "title": "Islām, īmān and iḥsān: the ḥadīth of Jibrīl", "narrator": "ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb", "source": "Muslim (8)", "ar": "عَنْ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ أَيْضًا قَالَ:  بَيْنَمَا نَحْنُ جُلُوسٌ عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ﷺ ذَاتَ يَوْمٍ، إذْ طَلَعَ عَلَيْنَا رَجُلٌ شَدِيدُ بَيَاضِ الثِّيَابِ، شَدِيدُ سَوَادِ الشَّعْرِ، لَا يُرَى عَلَيْهِ أَثَرُ السَّفَرِ، وَلَا يَعْرِفُهُ مِنَّا أَحَدٌ. حَتَّى جَلَسَ إلَى النَّبِيِّ ﷺ. فَأَسْنَدَ رُكْبَتَيْهِ إلَى رُكْبَتَيْهِ، وَوَضَعَ كَفَّيْهِ عَلَى فَخِذَيْهِ،\nوَقَالَ: يَا مُحَمَّدُ أَخْبِرْنِي عَنْ الْإِسْلَامِ.\nفَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ الْإِسْلَامُ أَنْ تَشْهَدَ أَنْ لَا إلَهَ إلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، وَتُقِيمَ الصَّلَاةَ، وَتُؤْتِيَ الزَّكَاةَ، وَتَصُومَ رَمَضَانَ، وَتَحُجَّ الْبَيْتَ إنْ اسْتَطَعْت إلَيْهِ سَبِيلًا.\nقَالَ: صَدَقْت. فَعَجِبْنَا لَهُ يَسْأَلُهُ وَيُصَدِّقُهُ!\nقَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنْ الْإِيمَانِ.\nقَالَ: أَنْ تُؤْمِنَ بِاَللَّهِ وَمَلَائِكَتِهِ وَكُتُبِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ، وَتُؤْمِنَ بِالْقَدَرِ خَيْرِهِ وَشَرِّهِ.\nقَالَ: صَدَقْت. قَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنْ الْإِحْسَانِ.\nقَالَ: أَنْ تَعْبُدَ اللَّهَ كَأَنَّك تَرَاهُ، فَإِنْ لَمْ تَكُنْ تَرَاهُ فَإِنَّهُ يَرَاك.\nقَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنْ السَّاعَةِ. قَالَ: مَا الْمَسْئُولُ عَنْهَا بِأَعْلَمَ مِنْ السَّائِلِ.\nقَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنْ أَمَارَاتِهَا؟ قَالَ: أَنْ تَلِدَ الْأَمَةُ رَبَّتَهَا، وَأَنْ تَرَى الْحُفَاةَ الْعُرَاةَ الْعَالَةَ رِعَاءَ الشَّاءِ يَتَطَاوَلُونَ فِي الْبُنْيَانِ. ثُمَّ انْطَلَقَ، فَلَبِثْتُ مَلِيًّا،\nثُمَّ قَالَ: يَا عُمَرُ أَتَدْرِي مَنْ السَّائِلُ؟\nقُلْتُ: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ.\nقَالَ: فَإِنَّهُ جِبْرِيلُ أَتَاكُمْ يُعَلِّمُكُمْ دِينَكُمْ", "en": "One day, while we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man appeared before us with very white clothes and very black hair. No sign of travel could be seen on him, and none of us knew him. He sat down facing the Prophet ﷺ, rested his knees against his knees, placed his palms on his thighs and said: “O Muḥammad, tell me about Islām.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Islām is that you testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish the prayer, pay the zakāh, fast Ramaḍān, and perform Ḥajj to the House if you are able to.” He said: “You have spoken truly.” We were amazed that he asked him and then confirmed his answer. He said: “Tell me about īmān.” He said: “That you believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers and the Last Day, and that you believe in the decree, its good and its bad.” He said: “You have spoken truly. Tell me about iḥsān.” He said: “That you worship Allah as though you see Him, and if you do not see Him, He certainly sees you.” He said: “Tell me about the Hour.” He said: “The one asked about it knows no more than the one asking.” He said: “Then tell me about its signs.” He said: “That the slave-woman gives birth to her mistress, and that you see barefoot, unclothed, destitute shepherds competing in building tall buildings.” Then he left, and I stayed a while. Then he said: “O ʿUmar, do you know who the questioner was?” I said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “That was Jibrīl. He came to teach you your religion.”", "lessons": ["The religion has three levels: islām (outward practice), īmān (inner belief) and iḥsān (worshipping with full awareness of Allah).", "Jibrīl taught the Companions by asking questions, showing that good questions are a way of learning.", "A scholar should say “I do not know” when he does not know: even the Prophet ﷺ did not know when the Hour will come.", "Iḥsān means worshipping Allah as if you see Him, and remembering that He always sees you."], "quiz": [["Who was the man who asked the questions?", "The angel Jibrīl", "A Bedouin from Najd", "A scholar from Yemen", "A Jewish rabbi"], ["What was strange about the man’s appearance?", "No sign of travel was on him", "He was wearing armour", "He was very old and weak", "He had come on a camel"], ["“That you worship Allah as though you see Him” describes:", "Iḥsān", "Islām", "Īmān", "Taqwā"], ["Belief in the decree (al-qadar) is listed under:", "Īmān", "Islām", "Iḥsān", "The signs of the Hour"], ["What did the Prophet ﷺ say about the time of the Hour?", "The one asked knows no more than the asker", "It will come after a thousand years", "It will come on a Monday", "Only Jibrīl knows its time"]]},
  {"n": 3, "title": "The five pillars of Islām", "narrator": "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (8) and Muslim (16)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: سَمِعْت رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ يَقُولُ:  بُنِيَ الْإِسْلَامُ عَلَى خَمْسٍ: شَهَادَةِ أَنْ لَا إلَهَ إلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، وَإِقَامِ الصَّلَاةِ، وَإِيتَاءِ الزَّكَاةِ، وَحَجِّ الْبَيْتِ، وَصَوْمِ رَمَضَانَ", "en": "I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Islām is built on five: testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing the prayer, paying the zakāh, Ḥajj to the House, and fasting Ramaḍān.”", "lessons": ["Islām is like a building, and these five are its pillars. Without them the building cannot stand.", "The shahādah comes first: every other act is built on sincere belief in Allah and following His Messenger ﷺ.", "The pillars combine the body (prayer, fasting), wealth (zakāh) and both together (Ḥajj).", "Other good deeds complete the building, but they cannot replace a missing pillar."], "quiz": [["The Prophet ﷺ compared Islām to:", "A building on five pillars", "A tree with five branches", "A river with five streams", "A road with five stages"], ["Which pillar is mentioned first?", "The two testimonies (shahādah)", "Establishing the prayer", "Paying the zakāh", "Fasting Ramaḍān"], ["Which pillar is mainly an act of wealth?", "Zakāh", "Prayer", "Fasting", "Shahādah"], ["In this narration, Ḥajj is mentioned:", "Before fasting Ramaḍān", "Before the prayer", "Before the shahādah", "Not at all"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar", "ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb", "Muʿādh ibn Jabal", "Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh"]]},
  {"n": 4, "title": "Creation in the womb and the decree", "narrator": "ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (3208) and Muslim (2643)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مَسْعُودٍ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: حَدَّثَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ -وَهُوَ الصَّادِقُ الْمَصْدُوقُ-: إنَّ أَحَدَكُمْ يُجْمَعُ خَلْقُهُ فِي بَطْنِ أُمِّهِ أَرْبَعِينَ يَوْمًا نُطْفَةً، ثُمَّ يَكُونُ عَلَقَةً مِثْلَ ذَلِكَ، ثُمَّ يَكُونُ مُضْغَةً مِثْلَ ذَلِكَ، ثُمَّ يُرْسَلُ إلَيْهِ الْمَلَكُ فَيَنْفُخُ فِيهِ الرُّوحَ، وَيُؤْمَرُ بِأَرْبَعِ كَلِمَاتٍ: بِكَتْبِ رِزْقِهِ، وَأَجَلِهِ، وَعَمَلِهِ، وَشَقِيٍّ أَمْ سَعِيدٍ؛ فَوَاَللَّهِ الَّذِي لَا إلَهَ غَيْرُهُ إنَّ أَحَدَكُمْ لَيَعْمَلُ بِعَمَلِ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ حَتَّى مَا يَكُونُ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَهَا إلَّا ذِرَاعٌ فَيَسْبِقُ عَلَيْهِ الْكِتَابُ فَيَعْمَلُ بِعَمَلِ أَهْلِ النَّارِ فَيَدْخُلُهَا. وَإِنَّ أَحَدَكُمْ لَيَعْمَلُ بِعَمَلِ أَهْلِ النَّارِ حَتَّى مَا يَكُونُ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَهَا إلَّا ذِرَاعٌ فَيَسْبِقُ عَلَيْهِ الْكِتَابُ فَيَعْمَلُ بِعَمَلِ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ فَيَدْخُلُهَا", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the truthful and the believed, told us: “The creation of each of you is gathered in his mother’s womb for forty days as a drop, then he becomes a clinging clot for the same period, then a lump of flesh for the same period. Then the angel is sent to him and blows the soul into him, and he is commanded with four words: to write his provision, his lifespan, his deeds, and whether he will be wretched or happy. By Allah, besides whom there is no god, one of you may do the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is only an arm’s length between him and it, then what was written overtakes him, and he does the deeds of the people of the Fire and enters it. And one of you may do the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is only an arm’s length between him and it, then what was written overtakes him, and he does the deeds of the people of Paradise and enters it.”", "lessons": ["Allah has written each person’s provision, lifespan, deeds and final end; nothing happens outside His knowledge and decree.", "Deeds are judged by how a person ends, so a believer should never feel safe from going astray, nor despair of anyone’s guidance.", "The decree does not remove effort: we act, and ask Allah for a good ending.", "Make the duʿāʾ of the righteous: “O Turner of hearts, keep my heart firm on Your religion.”"], "quiz": [["How many things does the angel write for each person?", "Four", "Two", "Three", "Seven"], ["Which of these is one of the things written?", "His provision (rizq)", "His tribe and family", "His language", "His country of birth"], ["Ibn Masʿūd described the Prophet ﷺ as:", "The truthful and the believed", "The trustworthy and the patient", "The merciful and the generous", "The leader and the guide"], ["The ḥadīth teaches that deeds are judged most by:", "How a person ends", "How a person begins", "How long a person lives", "How wealthy a person is"], ["What is blown into the child by the angel?", "The soul (rūḥ)", "The intellect", "The provision", "The faith (īmān)"]]},
  {"n": 5, "title": "Rejecting innovation in the religion", "narrator": "ʿĀʾishah, Mother of the Believers", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (2697) and Muslim (1718)", "ar": "عَنْ أُمِّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أُمِّ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا، قَالَتْ: قَالَ: رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ مَنْ أَحْدَثَ فِي أَمْرِنَا هَذَا مَا لَيْسَ مِنْهُ فَهُوَ رَدٌّ\nوَفِي رِوَايَةٍ لِمُسْلِمٍ: مَنْ عَمِلَ عَمَلًا لَيْسَ عَلَيْهِ أَمْرُنَا فَهُوَ رَدٌّ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever introduces into this matter of ours something that is not from it, it is rejected.” In a narration of Muslim: “Whoever does a deed that is not in accordance with our matter, it is rejected.”", "lessons": ["A deed is accepted only when it is sincere (ḥadīth 1) and in line with the Sunnah (this ḥadīth).", "“This matter of ours” means the religion: acts of worship must have a basis in the Qur’an and Sunnah.", "Good intentions do not make an invented act of worship acceptable.", "Worldly matters such as new technology are not innovation in the religion."], "quiz": [["What happens to a deed introduced into the religion that is not from it?", "It is rejected", "It is half rewarded", "It is accepted if well meant", "It becomes a sunnah"], ["“This matter of ours” refers to:", "The religion of Islām", "The rule of the caliph", "Trade in the market", "The customs of Makkah"], ["Together with ḥadīth 1, this ḥadīth shows a deed needs:", "Sincerity and following the Sunnah", "Witnesses and a written record", "Wealth and a good reputation", "Strength and a long life"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "ʿĀʾishah", "Umm Salamah", "Ḥafṣah", "Khadījah"], ["Which of these would NOT be called innovation in the religion?", "Using a phone to learn Qur’an", "Adding a sixth daily prayer", "Inventing a new form of ʿĪd", "Changing the number of rakʿahs"]]},
  {"n": 6, "title": "The lawful, the unlawful and the doubtful", "narrator": "an-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (52) and Muslim (1599)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ النُّعْمَانِ بْنِ بَشِيرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا، قَالَ: سَمِعْت رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ يَقُولُ: إنَّ الْحَلَالَ بَيِّنٌ، وَإِنَّ الْحَرَامَ بَيِّنٌ، وَبَيْنَهُمَا أُمُورٌ مُشْتَبِهَاتٌ لَا يَعْلَمُهُنَّ كَثِيرٌ مِنْ النَّاسِ، فَمَنْ اتَّقَى الشُّبُهَاتِ فَقَدْ اسْتَبْرَأَ لِدِينِهِ وَعِرْضِهِ، وَمَنْ وَقَعَ فِي الشُّبُهَاتِ وَقَعَ فِي الْحَرَامِ، كَالرَّاعِي يَرْعَى حَوْلَ الْحِمَى يُوشِكُ أَنْ يَرْتَعَ فِيهِ، أَلَا وَإِنَّ لِكُلِّ مَلِكٍ حِمًى، أَلَا وَإِنَّ حِمَى اللَّهِ مَحَارِمُهُ، أَلَا وَإِنَّ فِي الْجَسَدِ مُضْغَةً إذَا صَلَحَتْ صَلَحَ الْجَسَدُ كُلُّهُ، وَإذَا فَسَدَتْ فَسَدَ الْجَسَدُ كُلُّهُ، أَلَا وَهِيَ الْقَلْبُ", "en": "I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters which many people do not know. Whoever guards against the doubtful matters has protected his religion and his honour, and whoever falls into the doubtful matters falls into the unlawful, like a shepherd grazing around a sanctuary who is about to graze in it. Indeed every king has a sanctuary, and Allah’s sanctuary is what He has forbidden. Indeed in the body there is a lump of flesh: if it is sound, the whole body is sound, and if it is corrupt, the whole body is corrupt. Indeed, it is the heart.”", "lessons": ["Most rulings are clear; a smaller area is unclear to many people, and caution there protects your religion and reputation.", "Those with knowledge can clarify doubtful matters, so ask the people of knowledge.", "Small compromises lead to bigger ones, like a shepherd who grazes too close to a private pasture.", "The heart controls the body: work on it with sincerity, remembrance and avoiding sin."], "quiz": [["What lies between the clearly lawful and the clearly unlawful?", "Doubtful matters", "Disliked matters", "Recommended matters", "Forgotten matters"], ["Avoiding doubtful matters protects a person’s:", "Religion and honour", "Wealth and children", "Health and strength", "Home and land"], ["The person who falls into doubtful matters is compared to:", "A shepherd near a sanctuary", "A traveller without water", "A trader in a strange market", "A builder without tools"], ["What is “the sanctuary of Allah”?", "What He has forbidden", "The Kaʿbah and its mosque", "The city of Madinah", "The night of Qadr"], ["Which part of the body decides whether the rest is sound?", "The heart", "The tongue", "The mind", "The eyes"]]},
  {"n": 7, "title": "The religion is sincere advice", "narrator": "Tamīm ad-Dārī", "source": "Muslim (55)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي رُقَيَّةَ تَمِيمِ بْنِ أَوْسٍ الدَّارِيِّ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ ﷺ قَالَ: الدِّينُ النَّصِيحَةُ. قُلْنَا: لِمَنْ؟ قَالَ: لِلَّهِ، وَلِكِتَابِهِ، وَلِرَسُولِهِ، وَلِأَئِمَّةِ الْمُسْلِمِينَ وَعَامَّتِهِمْ.", "en": "The Prophet ﷺ said: “The religion is naṣīḥah (sincere advice and goodwill).” We said: “To whom?” He said: “To Allah, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the Muslims and to their common people.”", "lessons": ["Naṣīḥah means sincerely wanting good for someone and acting on it; the Prophet ﷺ described the whole religion with it.", "Naṣīḥah to Allah is worshipping Him sincerely; to His Book is reciting, understanding and acting on it; to His Messenger ﷺ is loving and following him.", "Advice to leaders is given respectfully and in the right way, and supporting them in good.", "Advice to ordinary Muslims includes teaching them, helping them and not cheating them."], "quiz": [["The Prophet ﷺ said the religion is:", "Sincere advice (naṣīḥah)", "Patience and prayer", "Knowledge and action", "Charity and fasting"], ["How many parties are mentioned for naṣīḥah?", "Five", "Three", "Four", "Six"], ["Naṣīḥah to the Book of Allah includes:", "Reciting it and acting on it", "Keeping it high on a shelf only", "Reading it only in Ramaḍān", "Owning several copies of it"], ["Which of these is naṣīḥah to the common Muslims?", "Teaching them and not cheating them", "Avoiding all contact with them", "Praising them whatever they do", "Exposing their private mistakes"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "Tamīm ad-Dārī", "Salmān al-Fārisī", "Bilāl ibn Rabāḥ", "Abū Dharr al-Ghifārī"]]},
  {"n": 8, "title": "The sanctity of a Muslim", "narrator": "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (25) and Muslim (22)", "ar": "عَنْ ابْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ قَالَ: أُمِرْتُ أَنْ أُقَاتِلَ النَّاسَ حَتَّى يَشْهَدُوا أَنْ لَا إلَهَ إلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، وَيُقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ، وَيُؤْتُوا الزَّكَاةَ؛ فَإِذَا فَعَلُوا ذَلِكَ عَصَمُوا مِنِّي دِمَاءَهُمْ وَأَمْوَالَهُمْ إلَّا بِحَقِّ الْإِسْلَامِ، وَحِسَابُهُمْ عَلَى اللَّهِ تَعَالَى", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish the prayer and pay the zakāh. If they do that, they have protected their blood and their wealth from me, except by the right of Islām, and their reckoning is with Allah the Exalted.”", "lessons": ["Whoever outwardly accepts Islām and its practices has his life and property protected; we judge by what is apparent.", "What is in people’s hearts is for Allah to judge, not for us to guess.", "Prayer and zakāh are so central that they are named alongside the shahādah.", "This ḥadīth concerns the authority of the Muslim state, not individuals acting on their own."], "quiz": [["Which two practices are named after the shahādah?", "Prayer and zakāh", "Fasting and Ḥajj", "Prayer and fasting", "Zakāh and Ḥajj"], ["What do people protect by accepting Islām and its practices?", "Their blood and wealth", "Their land and titles", "Their tribe and family", "Their trade and markets"], ["“Their reckoning is with Allah” means:", "What is in their hearts is His to judge", "They will never be questioned at all", "They must explain themselves to others", "They will be judged only by their rulers"], ["We judge people in this world by:", "What is apparent from them", "What we suspect in their hearts", "What others say about them", "Their family background"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar", "ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd", "Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī", "Ibn ʿAbbās"]]},
  {"n": 9, "title": "Do what you can, avoid what is forbidden", "narrator": "Abū Hurayrah", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (7288) and Muslim (1337)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ صَخْرٍ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: سَمِعْت رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ يَقُولُ: مَا نَهَيْتُكُمْ عَنْهُ فَاجْتَنِبُوهُ، وَمَا أَمَرْتُكُمْ بِهِ فَأْتُوا مِنْهُ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ، فَإِنَّمَا أَهْلَكَ الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ كَثْرَةُ مَسَائِلِهِمْ وَاخْتِلَافُهُمْ عَلَى أَنْبِيَائِهِمْ", "en": "I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “What I have forbidden you, avoid it; and what I have commanded you, do as much of it as you are able. What destroyed those before you was only their excessive questioning and their disagreeing with their prophets.”", "lessons": ["Prohibitions are to be left completely, since leaving something is within everyone’s ability.", "Commands are done according to ability: Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity.", "Asking to learn is good; asking to argue, to find loopholes or to make things harder is blameworthy.", "Disagreeing with the prophets destroyed earlier nations, so we follow the Sunnah without arguing against it."], "quiz": [["How should we treat what the Prophet ﷺ forbade?", "Avoid it completely", "Do it rarely", "Avoid it when we are able", "Leave it after we have tried it"], ["How should we treat what he commanded?", "Do as much as we are able", "Do it only once in life", "Do it only if others do it", "Do it after asking many questions"], ["What destroyed earlier nations, according to the ḥadīth?", "Excessive questions and opposing their prophets", "Poverty, famine and years of drought", "Long wars with neighbouring nations", "Forgetting their language and writing"], ["Which kind of question is blameworthy?", "A question asked to make things difficult", "A question asked to learn a ruling", "A question asked to understand a verse", "A question asked to correct a mistake"], ["This ḥadīth shows that Islām is built on:", "Ease and ability", "Hardship and strain", "Wealth and power", "Debate and argument"]]},
  {"n": 10, "title": "Allah is pure and accepts only what is pure", "narrator": "Abū Hurayrah", "source": "Muslim (1015)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ إنَّ اللَّهَ طَيِّبٌ لَا يَقْبَلُ إلَّا طَيِّبًا، وَإِنَّ اللَّهَ أَمَرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ بِمَا أَمَرَ بِهِ الْمُرْسَلِينَ فَقَالَ تَعَالَى: يَا أَيُّهَا الرُّسُلُ كُلُوا مِنْ الطَّيِّبَاتِ وَاعْمَلُوا صَالِحًا، وَقَالَ تَعَالَى: يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُلُوا مِنْ طَيِّبَاتِ مَا رَزَقْنَاكُمْ ثُمَّ ذَكَرَ الرَّجُلَ يُطِيلُ السَّفَرَ أَشْعَثَ أَغْبَرَ يَمُدُّ يَدَيْهِ إلَى السَّمَاءِ: يَا رَبِّ! يَا رَبِّ! وَمَطْعَمُهُ حَرَامٌ، وَمَشْرَبُهُ حَرَامٌ، وَمَلْبَسُهُ حَرَامٌ، وَغُذِّيَ بِالْحَرَامِ، فَأَنَّى يُسْتَجَابُ لَهُ؟", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah is pure (ṭayyib) and accepts only what is pure. Allah has commanded the believers with what He commanded the messengers. He said: ‘O messengers, eat from the good things and do righteous deeds’ (al-Muʾminūn 23:51), and He said: ‘O you who believe, eat from the good things We have provided you’ (al-Baqarah 2:172).” Then he mentioned a man who travels far, dishevelled and dusty, stretching his hands to the sky: “O Lord! O Lord!” while his food is unlawful, his drink is unlawful, his clothing is unlawful and he has been nourished with the unlawful. “So how can he be answered?”", "lessons": ["Allah accepts deeds, charity and earnings that are good and lawful.", "Lawful food and income are a condition for duʿāʾ being answered.", "Even a traveller in hardship, raising his hands, can be blocked from an answer by unlawful earnings.", "Check how you earn and what you consume; it affects your worship."], "quiz": [["What does Allah accept, according to this ḥadīth?", "Only what is pure and good", "Anything given in charity", "Whatever is done in public", "Only what is very costly"], ["The believers were commanded with what was commanded to:", "The messengers", "The angels", "The scholars", "The rulers"], ["Why was the travelling man’s duʿāʾ not answered?", "His food, drink and clothing were unlawful", "He did not raise his hands high enough", "He made duʿāʾ while still on a journey", "He asked for far too many things at once"], ["The travelling man is described as:", "Dishevelled and dusty", "Wealthy and proud", "Young and strong", "Sick and silent"], ["A lesson of this ḥadīth is that duʿāʾ is affected by:", "How we earn and what we consume", "The language in which we speak", "The time of year that we ask", "How loudly or quietly we speak"]]},
  {"n": 11, "title": "Leave what makes you doubt", "narrator": "al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, grandson of the Prophet ﷺ", "source": "At-Tirmidhī (2518), who said: ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ; and an-Nasāʾī (5711)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي مُحَمَّدٍ الْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيِّ بْنِ أَبِي طَالِبٍ سِبْطِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ﷺ وَرَيْحَانَتِهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا، قَالَ: حَفِظْت مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ﷺ دَعْ مَا يُرِيبُك إلَى مَا لَا يُرِيبُك.\nوَقَالَ التِّرْمِذِيُّ: حَدِيثٌ حَسَنٌ صَحِيحٌ", "en": "I memorised from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt.”", "lessons": ["When you are unsure whether something is right, choose the option you are sure about.", "Doubt unsettles the heart; certainty brings calm and peace.", "This applies to food, earnings, speech and acts of worship.", "It does not mean following baseless whispers (waswasah); it is about real doubt."], "quiz": [["What does the Prophet ﷺ tell us to do with what makes us doubt?", "Leave it for what is certain", "Do it and then repent", "Ask the first person we see", "Keep doing it until sure"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī", "Al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī", "ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib", "Fāṭimah bint Muḥammad"], ["The narrator was related to the Prophet ﷺ as his:", "Grandson", "Cousin", "Uncle", "Nephew"], ["This ḥadīth is NOT an instruction to:", "Follow constant baseless whispers", "Avoid doubtful earnings", "Choose what is certainly lawful", "Seek peace of heart"], ["Who recorded this ḥadīth and called it ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ?", "At-Tirmidhī", "Al-Bukhārī", "Mālik", "Abū Dāwūd"]]},
  {"n": 12, "title": "Leaving what does not concern you", "narrator": "Abū Hurayrah", "source": "At-Tirmidhī (2317), who said it is ḥasan; and Ibn Mājah (3976)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ مِنْ حُسْنِ إسْلَامِ الْمَرْءِ تَرْكُهُ مَا لَا يَعْنِيهِ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Part of the excellence of a person’s Islām is his leaving what does not concern him.”", "lessons": ["A good Muslim spends his time and words on what benefits his religion and his life.", "Gossip, prying into others’ affairs and idle talk weaken a person’s Islām.", "Social media makes this ḥadīth especially important: not every post deserves your attention.", "Leaving what does not concern you leaves more time for what does."], "quiz": [["Leaving what does not concern you is a sign of:", "The excellence of a person’s Islām", "Weak faith and a hard heart", "Pride and looking down on others", "A lack of knowledge of the religion"], ["Which of these is an example of “what does not concern you”?", "Prying into other people’s private affairs", "Learning how to pray correctly", "Caring for your elderly parents", "Earning a lawful living for your family"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "Abū Hurayrah", "Abū Bakr", "Abū ʿUbaydah", "Abū Mūsā"], ["A practical application today is to:", "Avoid time-wasting gossip and scrolling", "Stop speaking to people altogether", "Leave all worldly work and study", "Avoid asking teachers any questions"], ["At-Tirmidhī graded this ḥadīth:", "Ḥasan", "Mawḍūʿ", "Munkar", "Mursal"]]},
  {"n": 13, "title": "Love for your brother what you love for yourself", "narrator": "Anas ibn Mālik, servant of the Prophet ﷺ", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (13) and Muslim (45)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي حَمْزَةَ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ خَادِمِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ﷺ عَنْ النَّبِيِّ ﷺ قَالَ: لَا يُؤْمِنُ أَحَدُكُمْ حَتَّى يُحِبَّ لِأَخِيهِ مَا يُحِبُّ لِنَفْسِهِ", "en": "The Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you truly believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself.”", "lessons": ["Complete faith includes wanting good for others as you want it for yourself.", "This removes envy: you are happy when your brother receives good.", "It shows in action: sharing knowledge, giving advice and treating people fairly.", "Scholars say “brother” here includes all people in wanting guidance and good for them."], "quiz": [["According to this ḥadīth, complete faith requires:", "Loving for your brother what you love for yourself", "Praying the whole night through every single night", "Giving away all of your wealth to the poor at once", "Keeping away from everyone who is not like you"], ["Which quality does this ḥadīth remove from the heart?", "Envy", "Hope", "Fear of Allah", "Shyness"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "Anas ibn Mālik", "Mālik ibn Anas", "Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ", "Zayd ibn Thābit"], ["Anas was known as the Prophet’s ﷺ:", "Servant", "Scribe", "Guard", "Cousin"], ["Which action reflects this ḥadīth?", "Sharing useful knowledge with a classmate", "Hiding notes so others do worse", "Being sad when a friend succeeds", "Keeping good news to yourself"]]},
  {"n": 14, "title": "The sanctity of a Muslim’s life", "narrator": "ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (6878) and Muslim (1676)", "ar": "عَنْ ابْنِ مَسْعُودٍ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ لَا يَحِلُّ دَمُ امْرِئٍ مُسْلِمٍ إلَّا بِإِحْدَى ثَلَاثٍ: الثَّيِّبُ الزَّانِي، وَالنَّفْسُ بِالنَّفْسِ، وَالتَّارِكُ لِدِينِهِ الْمُفَارِقُ لِلْجَمَاعَةِ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The blood of a Muslim is not lawful except in one of three cases: the married person who commits adultery, a life for a life, and one who abandons his religion and separates from the community.”", "lessons": ["The life of a Muslim is sacred; the default is complete protection.", "The three exceptions are legal punishments, carried out only by a lawful authority after due process, never by individuals.", "This ḥadīth shows how seriously Islām guards life, family and the community."], "quiz": [["The blood of a Muslim becomes lawful in how many cases?", "Three", "Two", "Four", "Five"], ["“A life for a life” refers to:", "Retribution for deliberate murder", "The punishment for theft of goods", "Repayment of a debt that is owed", "Paying blood money for an accident"], ["Who may carry out these punishments?", "Only a lawful authority after due process", "Any Muslim who happens to see the crime", "The victim’s neighbours and relatives", "Anyone in the community who wishes to"], ["The default ruling for a Muslim’s life is:", "Complete protection", "It depends on his tribe", "It depends on his wealth", "No special protection"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd", "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr", "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar", "ʿAbdullāh ibn az-Zubayr"]]},
  {"n": 15, "title": "Speak good, honour your neighbour and guest", "narrator": "Abū Hurayrah", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (6018) and Muslim (47)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ قَالَ: مَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاَللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَلْيَقُلْ خَيْرًا أَوْ لِيَصْمُتْ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاَللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَلْيُكْرِمْ جَارَهُ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يُؤْمِنُ بِاَللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَلْيُكْرِمْ ضَيْفَهُ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or stay silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honour his neighbour. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honour his guest.”", "lessons": ["Before speaking, ask: is it good? If not, silence is better.", "Honouring neighbours includes kindness, help and not harming them with noise or rubbish.", "Honouring guests is a sign of faith: welcome them, feed them and serve them.", "Faith in the Last Day shows in manners, not only in belief."], "quiz": [["What should a believer do if he cannot speak good?", "Stay silent", "Speak quietly", "Speak only to friends", "Write it instead"], ["How many instructions are joined to faith in Allah and the Last Day?", "Three", "Two", "Four", "Five"], ["Which two people are we told to honour?", "The neighbour and the guest", "The teacher and the student", "The ruler and the judge", "The trader and the buyer"], ["This ḥadīth links good manners with:", "Belief in Allah and the Last Day", "Wealth and a high social status", "Age and long life experience", "Knowledge of poetry and history"], ["Which of these goes against honouring a neighbour?", "Playing loud music late at night", "Sending them food you cooked", "Greeting them warmly", "Visiting them when sick"]]},
  {"n": 16, "title": "Do not become angry", "narrator": "Abū Hurayrah", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (6116)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ رَجُلًا قَالَ لِلنَّبِيِّ ﷺ أَوْصِنِي. قَالَ: لَا تَغْضَبْ، فَرَدَّدَ مِرَارًا، قَالَ: لَا تَغْضَبْ", "en": "A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Advise me.” He said: “Do not become angry.” The man repeated his request several times, and each time he said: “Do not become angry.”", "lessons": ["Uncontrolled anger leads to many sins: harsh words, cutting ties, injustice and regret.", "Control anger by seeking refuge in Allah, staying silent, changing your position and making wuḍūʾ.", "Anger for Allah’s sake when His limits are violated is different from personal anger.", "Short advice repeated shows how important it is."], "quiz": [["What did the Prophet ﷺ advise the man?", "Do not become angry", "Pray at night", "Give charity", "Fast on Mondays"], ["How many times did the Prophet ﷺ give the advice?", "Several times, repeating it", "Only once, without repeating", "Exactly twice, then he left", "He did not answer the man"], ["Which of these helps calm anger?", "Seeking refuge in Allah from Shayṭān", "Raising your voice to be heard", "Making a quick and final decision", "Arguing until the other side gives in"], ["The repetition of the advice shows:", "How important it is", "The man did not hear", "The Prophet ﷺ was tired", "It was a joke"], ["Which ḥadīth collection recorded this ḥadīth?", "Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī", "Sunan Abī Dāwūd", "Muwaṭṭaʾ Mālik", "Sunan an-Nasāʾī"]]},
  {"n": 17, "title": "Excellence in everything", "narrator": "Shaddād ibn Aws", "source": "Muslim (1955)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي يَعْلَى شَدَّادِ بْنِ أَوْسٍ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ﷺ قَالَ: إنَّ اللَّهَ كَتَبَ الْإِحْسَانَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ، فَإِذَا قَتَلْتُمْ فَأَحْسِنُوا الْقِتْلَةَ، وَإِذَا ذَبَحْتُمْ فَأَحْسِنُوا الذِّبْحَةَ، وَلْيُحِدَّ أَحَدُكُمْ شَفْرَتَهُ، وَلْيُرِحْ ذَبِيحَتَهُ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has prescribed excellence (iḥsān) in everything. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let one of you sharpen his blade and spare his animal suffering.”", "lessons": ["Iḥsān is required in all things, from worship to work and even the treatment of animals.", "Islām forbids needless cruelty, even when an act is permitted.", "Practical care, such as sharpening the knife and not slaughtering in front of other animals, is part of the religion.", "Do every task as well as you can, because Allah has written excellence on all things."], "quiz": [["Allah has prescribed iḥsān (excellence) in:", "Everything", "Prayer only", "Charity only", "Fasting only"], ["What should a person do before slaughtering?", "Sharpen his blade", "Fast for a day", "Give charity", "Make wuḍūʾ"], ["The purpose of these instructions for slaughter is to:", "Spare the animal suffering", "Make the meat cheaper", "Make the work faster", "Keep the skin clean"], ["This ḥadīth shows Islām’s concern for:", "Mercy even to animals", "Hunting for sport", "Eating large amounts", "Selling livestock"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "Shaddād ibn Aws", "Saʿd ibn Muʿādh", "Usāmah ibn Zayd", "Khālid ibn al-Walīd"]]},
  {"n": 18, "title": "Taqwā wherever you are", "narrator": "Abū Dharr and Muʿādh ibn Jabal", "source": "At-Tirmidhī (1987), who said: ḥasan", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ جُنْدَبِ بْنِ جُنَادَةَ، وَأَبِي عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ مُعَاذِ بْنِ جَبَلٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا، عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ﷺ قَالَ: اتَّقِ اللَّهَ حَيْثُمَا كُنْت، وَأَتْبِعْ السَّيِّئَةَ الْحَسَنَةَ تَمْحُهَا، وَخَالِقْ النَّاسَ بِخُلُقٍ حَسَنٍ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fear Allah wherever you are, follow a bad deed with a good deed and it will wipe it out, and treat people with good character.”", "lessons": ["Taqwā is not only in the mosque: it is in private and public, at home, at school and online.", "When you slip, follow it quickly with a good deed and repentance.", "Good character with people is a core part of religion, not an extra.", "The ḥadīth covers your duty to Allah, to yourself and to others."], "quiz": [["Where should a believer have taqwā?", "Wherever he is", "Only in the mosque", "Only in Ramaḍān", "Only in public"], ["What wipes out a bad deed, according to this ḥadīth?", "A good deed that follows it", "Forgetting about it", "Telling people about it", "Waiting a long time"], ["How should we treat people?", "With good character", "With suspicion", "With silence", "With strictness only"], ["This ḥadīth was narrated by Abū Dharr and:", "Muʿādh ibn Jabal", "Abū Bakr", "Ubayy ibn Kaʿb", "Abū Ayyūb"], ["At-Tirmidhī graded it:", "Ḥasan", "Weak", "Fabricated", "Mursal"]]},
  {"n": 19, "title": "Be mindful of Allah, He will protect you", "narrator": "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās", "source": "At-Tirmidhī (2516), who said: ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ; the second narration is in Aḥmad", "ar": "عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَبَّاسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: كُنْت خَلْفَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ﷺ يَوْمًا، فَقَالَ: يَا غُلَامِ! إنِّي أُعَلِّمُك كَلِمَاتٍ: احْفَظْ اللَّهَ يَحْفَظْك، احْفَظْ اللَّهَ تَجِدْهُ تُجَاهَك، إذَا سَأَلْت فَاسْأَلْ اللَّهَ، وَإِذَا اسْتَعَنْت فَاسْتَعِنْ بِاَللَّهِ، وَاعْلَمْ أَنَّ الْأُمَّةَ لَوْ اجْتَمَعَتْ عَلَى أَنْ يَنْفَعُوك بِشَيْءٍ لَمْ يَنْفَعُوك إلَّا بِشَيْءٍ قَدْ كَتَبَهُ اللَّهُ لَك، وَإِنْ اجْتَمَعُوا عَلَى أَنْ يَضُرُّوك بِشَيْءٍ لَمْ يَضُرُّوك إلَّا بِشَيْءٍ قَدْ كَتَبَهُ اللَّهُ عَلَيْك؛ رُفِعَتْ الْأَقْلَامُ، وَجَفَّتْ الصُّحُفُ.\nوَفِي رِوَايَةِ غَيْرِ التِّرْمِذِيِّ: احْفَظْ اللَّهَ تَجِدْهُ أَمَامَك، تَعَرَّفْ إلَى اللَّهِ فِي الرَّخَاءِ يَعْرِفُك فِي الشِّدَّةِ، وَاعْلَمْ أَنَّ مَا أَخْطَأَك لَمْ يَكُنْ لِيُصِيبَك، وَمَا أَصَابَك لَمْ يَكُنْ لِيُخْطِئَك، وَاعْلَمْ أَنَّ النَّصْرَ مَعَ الصَّبْرِ، وَأَنْ الْفَرَجَ مَعَ الْكَرْبِ، وَأَنَّ مَعَ الْعُسْرِ يُسْرًا", "en": "I was behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day and he said: “Young man, I will teach you some words. Be mindful of Allah and He will protect you. Be mindful of Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah; and when you seek help, seek help from Allah. Know that if the whole nation gathered together to benefit you with something, they would not benefit you except with what Allah had already written for you; and if they gathered together to harm you with something, they would not harm you except with what Allah had already written against you. The pens have been lifted and the pages have dried.” In another narration: “Be mindful of Allah and you will find Him in front of you. Get to know Allah in times of ease and He will know you in times of hardship. Know that what missed you was never going to reach you, and what reached you was never going to miss you. Know that victory comes with patience, relief comes with hardship, and with difficulty comes ease.”", "lessons": ["“Be mindful of Allah” means guarding His commands and limits; in return He guards you.", "Ask Allah alone and rely on Him; people cannot benefit or harm you except by His decree.", "Remember Allah in easy times, and He will be with you in hard times.", "This advice was given to Ibn ʿAbbās when he was a boy: children can learn deep faith."], "quiz": [["How old was Ibn ʿAbbās when he heard this advice?", "A young boy", "An old man", "A middle-aged man", "A newborn"], ["“Be mindful of Allah and He will…”", "Protect you", "Make you rich", "Make you famous", "Make you a leader"], ["When you ask, ask:", "Allah", "Kings", "Rich people", "Elders"], ["If the whole nation gathered to harm you, they could only harm you with:", "What Allah had written against you", "What their leaders agreed on", "What they planned in secret", "Whatever they were able to do"], ["Which statement is in the second narration?", "Relief comes with hardship", "Wealth comes with patience", "Honour comes with poetry", "Strength comes with anger"]]},
  {"n": 20, "title": "Modesty (ḥayāʾ)", "narrator": "Abū Masʿūd ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmr al-Anṣārī", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (3483)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي مَسْعُودٍ عُقْبَةَ بْنِ عَمْرٍو الْأَنْصَارِيِّ الْبَدْرِيِّ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ إنَّ مِمَّا أَدْرَكَ النَّاسُ مِنْ كَلَامِ النُّبُوَّةِ الْأُولَى: إذَا لَمْ تَسْتَحِ فَاصْنَعْ مَا شِئْت", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the words people have received from the earliest prophecy is: if you feel no shame, then do as you wish.”", "lessons": ["Ḥayāʾ (modesty and a sense of shame) stops a person from doing what is wrong.", "This saying has been known since the earliest prophets: it is a shared message of revelation.", "It can be understood as a warning (a shameless person will do anything) or as a rule (if an act is not shameful, you may do it).", "Ḥayāʾ before Allah means not letting Him see you where He has forbidden."], "quiz": [["This saying comes from:", "The earliest prophecy", "Arab poetry", "Greek philosophy", "Persian kings"], ["The main quality praised in this ḥadīth is:", "Modesty (ḥayāʾ)", "Courage (shajāʿah)", "Generosity (karam)", "Eloquence (bayān)"], ["One meaning of the ḥadīth is a warning that:", "A shameless person will do anything", "Shyness stops a person from learning", "Every action is permitted to everyone", "Shame is a weakness to be overcome"], ["Another meaning is that:", "If an act is not shameful, you may do it", "You must avoid doing anything at all", "Only the prophets need to have modesty", "Modesty is needed only in public places"], ["Which collection recorded this ḥadīth?", "Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī", "Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim", "Sunan at-Tirmidhī", "Sunan Ibn Mājah"]]},
  {"n": 21, "title": "Say: I believe in Allah, then be steadfast", "narrator": "Sufyān ibn ʿAbdillāh ath-Thaqafī", "source": "Muslim (38)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي عَمْرٍو وَقِيلَ: أَبِي عَمْرَةَ سُفْيَانَ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قُلْت: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! قُلْ لِي فِي الْإِسْلَامِ قَوْلًا لَا أَسْأَلُ عَنْهُ أَحَدًا غَيْرَك؛ قَالَ: قُلْ: آمَنْت بِاَللَّهِ ثُمَّ اسْتَقِمْ", "en": "I said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me something about Islām that I will not need to ask anyone else about.” He said: “Say: I believe in Allah, then be steadfast.”", "lessons": ["The whole religion is summed up in two things: true faith and staying firm on it.", "Istiqāmah (steadfastness) means staying on the straight path in belief, worship and conduct.", "Consistency matters more than bursts of effort.", "Allah promises the steadfast that the angels will descend on them with reassurance (Fuṣṣilat 41:30)."], "quiz": [["What did the Prophet ﷺ tell Sufyān to say?", "I believe in Allah", "Allah is the Greatest", "Glory be to Allah", "There is no power except with Allah"], ["After faith, what did he tell him to do?", "Be steadfast", "Travel for knowledge", "Give charity", "Fight in the path of Allah"], ["Sufyān wanted advice that:", "He would not need to ask anyone else about", "Would make him wealthy within a short time", "Would be long enough to fill a whole book", "Only the greatest scholars could understand"], ["Istiqāmah means:", "Staying firm on the straight path", "Moving between opinions", "Being strict with others", "Leaving the world entirely"], ["Which collection recorded this ḥadīth?", "Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim", "Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī", "Sunan Abī Dāwūd", "Musnad Aḥmad"]]},
  {"n": 22, "title": "The obligations that lead to Paradise", "narrator": "Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī", "source": "Muslim (15)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ الْأَنْصَارِيِّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا: أَنَّ رَجُلًا سَأَلَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ فَقَالَ: أَرَأَيْت إذَا صَلَّيْت الْمَكْتُوبَاتِ، وَصُمْت رَمَضَانَ، وَأَحْلَلْت الْحَلَالَ، وَحَرَّمْت الْحَرَامَ، وَلَمْ أَزِدْ عَلَى ذَلِكَ شَيْئًا؛ أَأَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ", "en": "A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Tell me: if I pray the obligatory prayers, fast Ramaḍān, treat the lawful as lawful and the unlawful as unlawful, and do nothing more than that, will I enter Paradise?” He said: “Yes.”", "lessons": ["Doing the obligations and avoiding the prohibitions is the path to Paradise.", "“Treating the lawful as lawful” means believing it lawful; “treating the unlawful as unlawful” means believing it unlawful and avoiding it.", "Islām is achievable: the basic path is clear and within reach.", "Voluntary deeds raise your rank and make up for shortcomings in the obligations."], "quiz": [["What did the man ask about?", "Whether the obligations would admit him to Paradise", "How to perform the rites of Ḥajj and ʿUmrah", "Which things break the fast in Ramaḍān", "How to divide an inheritance among relatives"], ["What was the Prophet’s ﷺ answer?", "Yes", "No", "Only with extra prayers", "Only if he fights"], ["“Treating the unlawful as unlawful” means:", "Believing it unlawful and avoiding it", "Doing it only rarely and in private", "Doing it while feeling guilty about it", "Asking others about it before doing it"], ["This ḥadīth shows that the religion is:", "Clear and achievable", "Only for scholars", "Impossible to complete", "Only about prayer"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh", "Jarīr ibn ʿAbdillāh", "Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib", "Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim"]]},
  {"n": 23, "title": "Purity is half of faith", "narrator": "Abū Mālik al-Ashʿarī", "source": "Muslim (223)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي مَالِكٍ الْحَارِثِ بْنِ عَاصِمٍ الْأَشْعَرِيِّ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ الطَّهُورُ شَطْرُ الْإِيمَانِ، وَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ تَمْلَأُ الْمِيزَانَ، وَسُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ تَمْلَآنِ -أَوْ: تَمْلَأُ- مَا بَيْنَ السَّمَاءِ وَالْأَرْضِ، وَالصَّلَاةُ نُورٌ، وَالصَّدَقَةُ بُرْهَانٌ، وَالصَّبْرُ ضِيَاءٌ، وَالْقُرْآنُ حُجَّةٌ لَك أَوْ عَلَيْك، كُلُّ النَّاسِ يَغْدُو، فَبَائِعٌ نَفْسَهُ فَمُعْتِقُهَا أَوْ مُوبِقُهَا", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Purity is half of faith. Al-ḥamdu lillāh (praise be to Allah) fills the scale, and subḥān Allāh wal-ḥamdu lillāh fill (or: fills) what is between the heavens and the earth. Prayer is light, charity is proof, patience is radiance, and the Qur’an is an argument for you or against you. Everyone goes out in the morning and sells himself, either freeing himself or destroying himself.”", "lessons": ["Purity, of body and of heart, is a great part of faith.", "Small words of dhikr carry enormous weight on the scale.", "Prayer gives light, charity proves faith, and patience gives steady light through hardship.", "Every day is a trade: your deeds either free you or ruin you."], "quiz": [["What is described as half of faith?", "Purity (ṭuhūr)", "Prayer", "Charity", "Patience"], ["What fills the scale?", "Al-ḥamdu lillāh", "Lā ilāha illā Allāh", "Astaghfirullāh", "Allāhu akbar"], ["Charity is described as:", "Proof", "Light", "Radiance", "A shield"], ["The Qur’an is described as:", "An argument for you or against you", "A light given only to the scholars", "A book to be read only in Ramaḍān", "A means of increasing your wealth"], ["“Everyone goes out in the morning and sells himself” means:", "Each day our deeds free us or ruin us", "Everyone must work in the market", "Slavery was common", "People should travel daily"]]},
  {"n": 24, "title": "The prohibition of injustice", "narrator": "Abū Dharr al-Ghifārī", "source": "Muslim (2577)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ الْغِفَارِيِّ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ عَنْ النَّبِيِّ ﷺ فِيمَا يَرْوِيهِ عَنْ رَبِّهِ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى، أَنَّهُ قَالَ: يَا عِبَادِي: إنِّي حَرَّمْت الظُّلْمَ عَلَى نَفْسِي، وَجَعَلْته بَيْنَكُمْ مُحَرَّمًا؛ فَلَا تَظَالَمُوا. يَا عِبَادِي! كُلُّكُمْ ضَالٌّ إلَّا مَنْ هَدَيْته، فَاسْتَهْدُونِي أَهْدِكُمْ. يَا عِبَادِي! كُلُّكُمْ جَائِعٌ إلَّا مَنْ أَطْعَمْته، فَاسْتَطْعِمُونِي أُطْعِمْكُمْ. يَا عِبَادِي! كُلُّكُمْ عَارٍ إلَّا مَنْ كَسَوْته، فَاسْتَكْسُونِي أَكْسُكُمْ. يَا عِبَادِي! إنَّكُمْ تُخْطِئُونَ بِاللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ، وَأَنَا أَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًا؛ فَاسْتَغْفِرُونِي أَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ. يَا عِبَادِي! إنَّكُمْ لَنْ تَبْلُغُوا ضُرِّي فَتَضُرُّونِي، وَلَنْ تَبْلُغُوا نَفْعِي فَتَنْفَعُونِي. يَا عِبَادِي! لَوْ أَنَّ أَوَّلَكُمْ وَآخِرَكُمْ وَإِنْسَكُمْ وَجِنَّكُمْ كَانُوا عَلَى أَتْقَى قَلْبِ رَجُلٍ وَاحِدٍ مِنْكُمْ، مَا زَادَ ذَلِكَ فِي مُلْكِي شَيْئًا. يَا عِبَادِي! لَوْ أَنَّ أَوَّلَكُمْ وَآخِرَكُمْ وَإِنْسَكُمْ وَجِنَّكُمْ كَانُوا عَلَى أَفْجَرِ قَلْبِ رَجُلٍ وَاحِدٍ مِنْكُمْ، مَا نَقَصَ ذَلِكَ مِنْ مُلْكِي شَيْئًا. يَا عِبَادِي! لَوْ أَنَّ أَوَّلَكُمْ وَآخِرَكُمْ وَإِنْسَكُمْ وَجِنَّكُمْ قَامُوا فِي صَعِيدٍ وَاحِدٍ، فَسَأَلُونِي، فَأَعْطَيْت كُلَّ وَاحِدٍ مَسْأَلَته، مَا نَقَصَ ذَلِكَ مِمَّا عِنْدِي إلَّا كَمَا يَنْقُصُ الْمِخْيَطُ إذَا أُدْخِلَ الْبَحْرَ. يَا عِبَادِي! إنَّمَا هِيَ أَعْمَالُكُمْ أُحْصِيهَا لَكُمْ، ثُمَّ أُوَفِّيكُمْ إيَّاهَا؛ فَمَنْ وَجَدَ خَيْرًا فَلْيَحْمَدْ اللَّهَ، وَمَنْ وَجَدَ غَيْرَ ذَلِكَ فَلَا يَلُومَن إلَّا نَفْسَهُ", "en": "The Prophet ﷺ narrated from his Lord: “O My servants, I have forbidden injustice for Myself and made it forbidden among you, so do not wrong one another. O My servants, all of you are astray except those I guide, so seek guidance from Me and I will guide you. O My servants, all of you are hungry except those I feed, so seek food from Me and I will feed you. O My servants, all of you are naked except those I clothe, so seek clothing from Me and I will clothe you. O My servants, you sin by night and by day, and I forgive all sins, so seek forgiveness from Me and I will forgive you. O My servants, you cannot reach harming Me so as to harm Me, and you cannot reach benefiting Me so as to benefit Me. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, were as pious as the most pious heart of any one of you, that would not add anything to My dominion. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, were as wicked as the most wicked heart of any one of you, that would not decrease anything from My dominion. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, stood on one plain and asked of Me, and I gave each one what he asked, that would not decrease what I have except as a needle decreases the sea when it is dipped into it. O My servants, it is only your deeds that I record for you and then repay you for. So whoever finds good, let him praise Allah, and whoever finds other than that, let him blame no one but himself.”", "lessons": ["This is a ḥadīth qudsī: the Prophet ﷺ relates words from Allah.", "Allah forbade injustice for Himself; we must never wrong anyone.", "Every blessing, guidance, food, clothing and forgiveness, is from Allah, so ask Him for everything.", "Our obedience does not benefit Allah and our sins do not harm Him; they benefit or harm only us."], "quiz": [["What kind of ḥadīth is this?", "A ḥadīth qudsī", "A ḥadīth mursal", "A weak ḥadīth", "A saying of a Companion"], ["What has Allah forbidden for Himself?", "Injustice", "Mercy", "Forgiveness", "Generosity"], ["If everyone asked Allah and He gave each person, His treasure would decrease only like:", "A needle dipped in the sea", "A cup taken from a river", "A grain taken from a sack", "A leaf falling from a tree"], ["Do our good deeds benefit Allah?", "No, they benefit only us", "Yes, they increase His kingdom", "Only the good deeds of prophets", "Only deeds done in Makkah"], ["Whoever finds other than good should blame:", "No one but himself", "His parents", "His teachers", "The decree of Allah"]]},
  {"n": 25, "title": "Every good deed is charity", "narrator": "Abū Dharr al-Ghifārī", "source": "Muslim (1006)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ أَيْضًا، أَنَّ نَاسًا مِنْ أَصْحَابِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ﷺ قَالُوا لِلنَّبِيِّ ﷺ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ذَهَبَ أَهْلُ الدُّثُورِ بِالْأُجُورِ؛ يُصَلُّونَ كَمَا نُصَلِّي، وَيَصُومُونَ كَمَا نَصُومُ، وَيَتَصَدَّقُونَ بِفُضُولِ أَمْوَالِهِمْ. قَالَ: أَوَلَيْسَ قَدْ جَعَلَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ مَا تَصَّدَّقُونَ؟ إنَّ بِكُلِّ تَسْبِيحَةٍ صَدَقَةً، وَكُلِّ تَكْبِيرَةٍ صَدَقَةً، وَكُلِّ تَحْمِيدَةٍ صَدَقَةً، وَكُلِّ تَهْلِيلَةٍ صَدَقَةً، وَأَمْرٌ بِمَعْرُوفٍ صَدَقَةٌ، وَنَهْيٌ عَنْ مُنْكَرٍ صَدَقَةٌ، وَفِي بُضْعِ أَحَدِكُمْ صَدَقَةٌ. قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَيَأْتِي أَحَدُنَا شَهْوَتَهُ وَيَكُونُ لَهُ فِيهَا أَجْرٌ؟ قَالَ: أَرَأَيْتُمْ لَوْ وَضَعَهَا فِي حَرَامٍ أَكَانَ عَلَيْهِ وِزْرٌ؟ فَكَذَلِكَ إذَا وَضَعَهَا فِي الْحَلَالِ، كَانَ لَهُ أَجْرٌ", "en": "Some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “O Messenger of Allah, the wealthy have taken all the reward. They pray as we pray, fast as we fast, and give charity from their extra wealth.” He said: “Has Allah not given you things to give in charity? Every tasbīḥ is charity, every takbīr is charity, every taḥmīd is charity, every tahlīl is charity, enjoining good is charity, forbidding evil is charity, and in the intimacy of one of you with his wife there is charity.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, does one of us fulfil his desire and get a reward for it?” He said: “Do you not see that if he did it in the unlawful, he would bear a sin? So likewise, if he does it in the lawful, he has a reward.”", "lessons": ["The poor Companions competed in good deeds, not in wealth.", "Dhikr and enjoining good are charity open to everyone, rich or poor.", "Lawful acts done with a good intention, even meeting one’s desires in marriage, are rewarded.", "Choosing the lawful over the unlawful is itself worship."], "quiz": [["What did the poor Companions complain about?", "The wealthy had more chances to give charity", "They could not pray in the mosque", "They had no time to learn", "They were not allowed to fight"], ["Which of these did the Prophet ﷺ call charity?", "Saying subḥān Allāh", "Sleeping late", "Buying new clothes", "Travelling for trade"], ["Enjoining good and forbidding evil are:", "Charity", "Only for rulers", "Only for scholars", "Unrewarded"], ["Why is a lawful marriage relationship rewarded?", "Because doing it unlawfully would be a sin", "Because it is difficult and needs effort", "Because it costs a great deal of money", "Because other people come to know of it"], ["The lesson of this ḥadīth is that:", "Many kinds of good deeds are open to all", "Only the wealthy can earn great reward", "Charity is only ever a gift of money", "Dhikr is good but carries no reward"]]},
  {"n": 26, "title": "Charity for every joint", "narrator": "Abū Hurayrah", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (2989) and Muslim (1009)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ كُلُّ سُلَامَى مِنْ النَّاسِ عَلَيْهِ صَدَقَةٌ، كُلَّ يَوْمٍ تَطْلُعُ فِيهِ الشَّمْسُ تَعْدِلُ بَيْنَ اثْنَيْنِ صَدَقَةٌ، وَتُعِينُ الرَّجُلَ فِي دَابَّتِهِ فَتَحْمِلُهُ عَلَيْهَا أَوْ تَرْفَعُ لَهُ عَلَيْهَا مَتَاعَهُ صَدَقَةٌ، وَالْكَلِمَةُ الطَّيِّبَةُ صَدَقَةٌ، وَبِكُلِّ خُطْوَةٍ تَمْشِيهَا إلَى الصَّلَاةِ صَدَقَةٌ، وَتُمِيطُ الْأَذَى عَنْ الطَّرِيقِ صَدَقَةٌ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Charity is due on every joint of a person, every day the sun rises. Judging justly between two people is charity. Helping a man with his mount, lifting him onto it or lifting his belongings onto it, is charity. A good word is charity. Every step you take to the prayer is charity. Removing something harmful from the road is charity.”", "lessons": ["Each of our joints is a blessing, and thanks for them is due every day.", "Charity is not only money: justice, help, kind words and walking to prayer are all charity.", "Small, everyday acts of service carry great reward.", "Removing harm from the road shows care for the community."], "quiz": [["Charity is due on every:", "Joint of a person", "Coin a person owns", "Meal a person eats", "Friend a person has"], ["How often is this charity due?", "Every day the sun rises", "Once a year", "Every Friday", "Only in Ramaḍān"], ["Which of these is NOT mentioned as charity?", "Building a house", "A good word", "Removing harm from the road", "Judging justly between two people"], ["Every step taken to the prayer is:", "Charity", "A sin removed only", "Not counted", "Only for men"], ["The main lesson is that charity includes:", "Many acts of service, not only money", "Only the zakāh paid once each year", "Only gifts given to close family", "Only food that is given to the poor"]]},
  {"n": 27, "title": "Righteousness and sin", "narrator": "an-Nawwās ibn Samʿān and Wābiṣah ibn Maʿbad", "source": "Muslim (2553); the second narration is in Aḥmad and ad-Dārimī, graded ḥasan by an-Nawawī", "ar": "عَنْ النَّوَّاسِ بْنِ سَمْعَانَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ عَنْ النَّبِيِّ ﷺ قَالَ: الْبِرُّ حُسْنُ الْخُلُقِ، وَالْإِثْمُ مَا حَاكَ فِي صَدْرِك، وَكَرِهْت أَنْ يَطَّلِعَ عَلَيْهِ النَّاسُ\nوَعَنْ وَابِصَةَ بْنِ مَعْبَدٍ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: أَتَيْت رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ فَقَالَ: جِئْتَ تَسْأَلُ عَنْ الْبِرِّ؟ قُلْت: نَعَمْ. فَقَالَ: اسْتَفْتِ قَلْبَك، الْبِرُّ مَا اطْمَأَنَّتْ إلَيْهِ النَّفْسُ، وَاطْمَأَنَّ إلَيْهِ الْقَلْبُ، وَالْإِثْمُ مَا حَاكَ فِي النَّفْسِ وَتَرَدَّدَ فِي الصَّدْرِ، وَإِنْ أَفْتَاك النَّاسُ وَأَفْتَوْك", "en": "The Prophet ﷺ said: “Righteousness is good character, and sin is what wavers in your heart and you dislike people finding out about it.” And Wābiṣah said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: “You have come to ask about righteousness?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “Consult your heart. Righteousness is what the soul feels at ease with and the heart feels at ease with, and sin is what wavers in the soul and moves back and forth in the chest, even if people give you rulings and give you rulings again.”", "lessons": ["Good character is at the heart of righteousness (birr).", "A sound heart feels uneasy about sin and wants to hide it.", "This applies to a believer whose heart is alive with faith, and to unclear matters; clear rulings of the Sharīʿah come first.", "If something troubles your conscience, do not let people’s permission override it."], "quiz": [["How did the Prophet ﷺ define righteousness (birr)?", "Good character", "Long prayers", "Many fasts", "Great wealth"], ["Sin is what you dislike that people:", "Find out about", "Praise you for", "Ask you about", "Help you with"], ["What did the Prophet ﷺ tell Wābiṣah to consult?", "His heart", "His tribe", "His books", "His friends"], ["How did the Prophet ﷺ know Wābiṣah’s question?", "He told him before he asked", "Wābiṣah wrote it down", "A Companion told him", "He heard it the day before"], ["“Consult your heart” applies mainly to:", "Unclear matters, for a believer with a sound heart", "Clear obligations such as the five daily prayers", "Rulings stated plainly in the Qur’an and Sunnah", "Matters that the scholars have agreed upon"]]},
  {"n": 28, "title": "Hold fast to the Sunnah", "narrator": "al-ʿIrbāḍ ibn Sāriyah", "source": "Abū Dāwūd (4607) and at-Tirmidhī (2676), who said: ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي نَجِيحٍ الْعِرْبَاضِ بْنِ سَارِيَةَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: وَعَظَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ مَوْعِظَةً وَجِلَتْ مِنْهَا الْقُلُوبُ، وَذَرَفَتْ مِنْهَا الْعُيُونُ، فَقُلْنَا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! كَأَنَّهَا مَوْعِظَةُ مُوَدِّعٍ فَأَوْصِنَا، قَالَ: أُوصِيكُمْ بِتَقْوَى اللَّهِ، وَالسَّمْعِ وَالطَّاعَةِ وَإِنْ تَأَمَّرَ عَلَيْكُمْ عَبْدٌ، فَإِنَّهُ مَنْ يَعِشْ مِنْكُمْ فَسَيَرَى اخْتِلَافًا كَثِيرًا، فَعَلَيْكُمْ بِسُنَّتِي وَسُنَّةِ الْخُلَفَاءِ الرَّاشِدِينَ الْمَهْدِيينَ، عَضُّوا عَلَيْهَا بِالنَّوَاجِذِ، وَإِيَّاكُمْ وَمُحْدَثَاتِ الْأُمُورِ؛ فَإِنَّ كُلَّ بِدْعَةٍ ضَلَالَةٌ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon that made our hearts fearful and our eyes weep. We said: “O Messenger of Allah, it is as if this is a farewell sermon, so advise us.” He said: “I advise you to fear Allah, and to listen and obey even if a slave is placed in authority over you. Whoever among you lives will see much disagreement, so hold to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs. Bite onto it with your molar teeth. And beware of newly invented matters, for every innovation is misguidance.”", "lessons": ["The Prophet’s ﷺ final advice centres on taqwā, unity and following the Sunnah.", "Disagreement will come; the way out is holding firmly to the Sunnah and the way of the rightly guided caliphs.", "“Bite onto it with your molars” means hold on as tightly as possible.", "Innovation in religion leads people away from guidance."], "quiz": [["How did the Companions describe the sermon?", "Like a farewell sermon", "Like a sermon for ʿĪd", "Like a sermon for war", "Like a wedding speech"], ["What was the first thing the Prophet ﷺ advised?", "Fear of Allah (taqwā)", "Travelling for knowledge", "Giving charity", "Learning poetry"], ["Whose Sunnah did he tell us to hold to, besides his own?", "The rightly guided caliphs", "The kings of Persia", "The poets of Quraysh", "Any famous scholar"], ["“Bite onto it with your molar teeth” means:", "Hold on as tightly as possible", "Eat carefully", "Speak less", "Be patient with hunger"], ["What did he say about every innovation in religion?", "It is misguidance", "It is sometimes good", "It is half rewarded", "It is allowed for scholars"]]},
  {"n": 29, "title": "The deeds that lead to Paradise, and the tongue", "narrator": "Muʿādh ibn Jabal", "source": "At-Tirmidhī (2616), who said: ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ", "ar": "عَنْ مُعَاذِ بْنِ جَبَلٍ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قُلْت يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! أَخْبِرْنِي بِعَمَلٍ يُدْخِلُنِي الْجَنَّةَ وَيُبَاعِدُنِي مِنْ النَّارِ، قَالَ: لَقَدْ سَأَلْت عَنْ عَظِيمٍ، وَإِنَّهُ لَيَسِيرٌ عَلَى مَنْ يَسَّرَهُ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ: تَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ لَا تُشْرِكْ بِهِ شَيْئًا، وَتُقِيمُ الصَّلَاةَ، وَتُؤْتِي الزَّكَاةَ، وَتَصُومُ رَمَضَانَ، وَتَحُجُّ الْبَيْتَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا أَدُلُّك عَلَى أَبْوَابِ الْخَيْرِ؟ الصَّوْمُ جُنَّةٌ، وَالصَّدَقَةُ تُطْفِئُ الْخَطِيئَةَ كَمَا يُطْفِئُ الْمَاءُ النَّارَ، وَصَلَاةُ الرَّجُلِ فِي جَوْفِ اللَّيْلِ، ثُمَّ تَلَا:  تَتَجَافَى جُنُوبُهُمْ عَنِ الْمَضَاجِعِ  حَتَّى بَلَغَ يَعْمَلُونَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا أُخْبِرُك بِرَأْسِ الْأَمْرِ وَعَمُودِهِ وَذُرْوَةِ سَنَامِهِ؟ قُلْت: بَلَى يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. قَالَ: رَأْسُ الْأَمْرِ الْإِسْلَامُ، وَعَمُودُهُ الصَّلَاةُ، وَذُرْوَةُ سَنَامِهِ الْجِهَادُ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا أُخْبِرُك بِمَلَاكِ ذَلِكَ كُلِّهِ؟ فَقُلْت: بَلَى يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ! فَأَخَذَ بِلِسَانِهِ وَقَالَ: كُفَّ عَلَيْك هَذَا. قُلْت: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ وَإِنَّا لَمُؤَاخَذُونَ بِمَا نَتَكَلَّمُ بِهِ؟ فَقَالَ: ثَكِلَتْك أُمُّك وَهَلْ يَكُبُّ النَّاسَ عَلَى وُجُوهِهِمْ -أَوْ قَالَ عَلَى مَنَاخِرِهِمْ- إلَّا حَصَائِدُ أَلْسِنَتِهِمْ؟!", "en": "I said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire.” He said: “You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for whoever Allah makes it easy for. Worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish the prayer, pay the zakāh, fast Ramaḍān and perform Ḥajj to the House.” Then he said: “Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Fasting is a shield; charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire; and a man’s prayer in the depth of the night.” Then he recited: “Their sides forsake their beds…” until he reached “…what they used to do” (as-Sajdah 32:16–17). Then he said: “Shall I not tell you of the head of the matter, its pillar and its peak?” I said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “The head of the matter is Islām, its pillar is the prayer, and its peak is jihād.” Then he said: “Shall I not tell you of what controls all of that?” I said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He took hold of his tongue and said: “Restrain this.” I said: “O Prophet of Allah, will we be held to account for what we say?” He said: “May your mother lose you, Muʿādh! Is there anything that throws people on their faces (or he said: on their noses) into the Fire other than the harvest of their tongues?”", "lessons": ["Paradise is great, but the path is easy for those Allah helps: the pillars of Islām first.", "The gates of goodness are fasting, charity and night prayer.", "Prayer is the pillar of the religion.", "Controlling the tongue protects all your other good deeds."], "quiz": [["What did Muʿādh ask the Prophet ﷺ?", "A deed that admits to Paradise and keeps from the Fire", "A way to become wealthy and respected among people", "Who would lead the Muslims after the Prophet ﷺ", "When exactly the Hour will come and what precedes it"], ["Fasting is described as:", "A shield", "A light", "A proof", "A ladder"], ["Charity extinguishes sin as:", "Water extinguishes fire", "Wind blows away dust", "The sun dries rain", "Night ends the day"], ["What is the pillar of the matter?", "The prayer", "Fasting", "Charity", "Ḥajj"], ["What did the Prophet ﷺ say controls all of that?", "Restraining the tongue", "Waking at night", "Giving all your wealth", "Travelling for knowledge"]]},
  {"n": 30, "title": "The limits set by Allah", "narrator": "Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī", "source": "Ad-Dāraquṭnī in his Sunan and others; graded ḥasan by an-Nawawī", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي ثَعْلَبَةَ الْخُشَنِيِّ جُرْثُومِ بن نَاشِر رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ﷺ قَال: إنَّ اللَّهَ تَعَالَى فَرَضَ فَرَائِضَ فَلَا تُضَيِّعُوهَا، وَحَدَّ حُدُودًا فَلَا تَعْتَدُوهَا، وَحَرَّمَ أَشْيَاءَ فَلَا تَنْتَهِكُوهَا، وَسَكَتَ عَنْ أَشْيَاءَ رَحْمَةً لَكُمْ غَيْرَ نِسْيَانٍ فَلَا تَبْحَثُوا عَنْهَا", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah the Exalted has laid down obligations, so do not neglect them. He has set limits, so do not overstep them. He has forbidden things, so do not violate them. And He has remained silent about things, out of mercy for you, not out of forgetfulness, so do not go searching into them.”", "lessons": ["Rulings fall into four groups: obligations, limits, prohibitions and things left unaddressed.", "What Allah left unaddressed is a mercy: the default in worldly matters is permissibility.", "Allah does not forget; His silence is deliberate.", "Do not make the religion harder by digging into matters left open."], "quiz": [["What should we do with the obligations Allah laid down?", "Not neglect them", "Do them only sometimes", "Change them when needed", "Leave them to scholars"], ["Why did Allah stay silent about some things?", "Out of mercy for us", "Out of forgetfulness", "Because they are unimportant", "Because they are secret"], ["What should we do about things Allah left unaddressed?", "Not go searching into them", "Treat them as forbidden", "Ask about them constantly", "Make new rules for them"], ["The “limits” of Allah should not be:", "Overstepped", "Learned", "Taught", "Remembered"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī", "Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī", "Abū Qatādah", "Abū Ṭalḥah"]]},
  {"n": 31, "title": "Be detached from the world", "narrator": "Sahl ibn Saʿd as-Sāʿidī", "source": "Ibn Mājah (4102) and others; graded ḥasan by an-Nawawī", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي الْعَبَّاسِ سَهْلِ بْنِ سَعْدٍ السَّاعِدِيّ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: جَاءَ رَجُلٌ إلَى النَّبِيِّ ﷺ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللهِ! دُلَّنِي عَلَى عَمَلٍ إذَا عَمِلْتُهُ أَحَبَّنِي اللهُ وَأَحَبَّنِي النَّاسُ؛ فَقَالَ: ازْهَدْ فِي الدُّنْيَا يُحِبَّك اللهُ، وَازْهَدْ فِيمَا عِنْدَ النَّاسِ يُحِبَّك النَّاسُ", "en": "A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, direct me to a deed which, if I do it, Allah will love me and people will love me.” He said: “Be detached from this world and Allah will love you, and be detached from what people have and people will love you.”", "lessons": ["Zuhd is not giving everything away; it is not letting the world own your heart.", "Allah loves the one whose heart is attached to the Hereafter.", "People love the one who does not look at what is in their hands or envy them.", "Use the world as a means, not a goal."], "quiz": [["What did the man want?", "A deed that makes Allah and people love him", "A way to become rich within a short time", "A way to defeat his enemies in battle", "A cure for an illness he was suffering"], ["To be loved by Allah, the Prophet ﷺ said:", "Be detached from this world", "Be famous among people", "Build many houses", "Travel widely"], ["To be loved by people, he said:", "Be detached from what people have", "Give people many gifts and favours", "Praise people often in their presence", "Agree with everyone about everything"], ["Zuhd means:", "Not letting the world own your heart", "Refusing all work and trade completely", "Living alone without a wife or family", "Never eating good or pleasant food"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "Sahl ibn Saʿd", "Saʿd ibn Muʿādh", "Saʿīd ibn Zayd", "Suhayl ibn ʿAmr"]]},
  {"n": 32, "title": "No harm and no reciprocating harm", "narrator": "Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī", "source": "Ibn Mājah and ad-Dāraquṭnī; Mālik narrated it in the Muwaṭṭaʾ as mursal; its routes strengthen one another", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ سَعْدِ بْنِ مَالِكِ بْنِ سِنَانٍ الْخُدْرِيّ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ قَالَ:  لَا ضَرَرَ وَلَا ضِرَارَ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is to be no harm and no reciprocating harm.”", "lessons": ["This short ḥadīth is a major principle of Islamic law: harm must be removed.", "You may not harm others, and you may not answer harm with greater harm.", "It applies to neighbours, trade, family, roads and public spaces.", "Scholars derived many legal maxims from it, such as “harm is to be removed”."], "quiz": [["What does this ḥadīth forbid?", "Harming others and answering harm with harm", "Asking a judge for one’s rights to be given", "Defending oneself lawfully when attacked", "Seeking justice in court against a wrongdoer"], ["This ḥadīth is famous as:", "A major principle of Islamic law", "A ḥadīth about prayer", "A story about the Prophets", "A duʿāʾ for travel"], ["Which legal maxim comes from it?", "Harm is to be removed", "Custom is never valid", "Certainty is removed by doubt", "Hardship brings difficulty"], ["Mālik narrated this ḥadīth in:", "The Muwaṭṭaʾ", "Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī", "Sunan Abī Dāwūd", "Musnad Aḥmad"], ["Who narrated it from the Prophet ﷺ in Ibn Mājah’s chain?", "Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī", "Abū Hurayrah", "Ibn ʿAbbās", "ʿĀʾishah"]]},
  {"n": 33, "title": "The burden of proof", "narrator": "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās", "source": "Al-Bayhaqī with this wording; part of it is in al-Bukhārī and Muslim", "ar": "عَنْ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ قَالَ: لَوْ يُعْطَى النَّاسُ بِدَعْوَاهُمْ لَادَّعَى رِجَالٌ أَمْوَالَ قَوْمٍ وَدِمَاءَهُمْ، لَكِنَّ الْبَيِّنَةَ عَلَى الْمُدَّعِي، وَالْيَمِينَ عَلَى مَنْ أَنْكَرَ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If people were given according to their claims, some men would claim the wealth and blood of others. But the proof is upon the claimant, and the oath is upon the one who denies.”", "lessons": ["Claims alone are not enough; justice needs evidence.", "The one who makes a claim must bring proof; the one who denies may take an oath.", "This protects people’s wealth, lives and honour from false accusations.", "It is a foundation of the Islamic justice system."], "quiz": [["What would happen if people were given according to their claims?", "Some would claim others’ wealth and blood", "Everyone would become honest and truthful", "Courts and judges would no longer be needed", "Nothing would change in how people behave"], ["On whom is the proof?", "The claimant", "The judge", "The one who denies", "The witnesses’ families"], ["On whom is the oath?", "The one who denies", "The claimant", "The judge", "The ruler"], ["This ḥadīth protects people from:", "False accusations", "Paying zakāh", "Lawful trade", "Inheritance"], ["Which collection has this exact wording?", "Al-Bayhaqī", "Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī", "Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim", "Muwaṭṭaʾ Mālik"]]},
  {"n": 34, "title": "Changing what is wrong", "narrator": "Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī", "source": "Muslim (49)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيّ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ سَمِعْت رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ يَقُولُ: مَنْ رَأَى مِنْكُمْ مُنْكَرًا فَلْيُغَيِّرْهُ بِيَدِهِ، فَإِنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَبِلِسَانِهِ، فَإِنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَبِقَلْبِهِ، وَذَلِكَ أَضْعَفُ الْإِيمَانِ", "en": "I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever among you sees something wrong, let him change it with his hand; if he is not able, then with his tongue; and if he is not able, then with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith.”", "lessons": ["Every Muslim has a duty to respond to wrong according to his ability.", "Changing with the hand is for those with authority over the matter, such as a parent at home or a ruler.", "Changing with the tongue should be done with wisdom and gentle words.", "Hating the wrong in the heart is the minimum; whoever does not even dislike it has a problem with his faith."], "quiz": [["How many levels of changing wrong are mentioned?", "Three", "Two", "Four", "Five"], ["The first level is changing it with:", "The hand", "The tongue", "The heart", "A letter"], ["Changing it with the heart is described as:", "The weakest of faith", "The best of faith", "Not part of faith", "Only for scholars"], ["Changing with the hand is mainly for those who:", "Have authority over the matter", "Are the strongest in the crowd", "Are the oldest in the gathering", "Are the wealthiest in the town"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī", "Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī", "Abū Dardāʾ", "Abū Bakrah"]]},
  {"n": 35, "title": "The brotherhood of Muslims", "narrator": "Abū Hurayrah", "source": "Muslim (2564)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ  لَا تَحَاسَدُوا، وَلَا تَنَاجَشُوا، وَلَا تَبَاغَضُوا، وَلَا تَدَابَرُوا، وَلَا يَبِعْ بَعْضُكُمْ عَلَى بَيْعِ بَعْضٍ، وَكُونُوا عِبَادَ اللَّهِ إخْوَانًا، الْمُسْلِمُ أَخُو الْمُسْلِمِ، لَا يَظْلِمُهُ، وَلَا يَخْذُلُهُ، وَلَا يَكْذِبُهُ، وَلَا يَحْقِرُهُ، التَّقْوَى هَاهُنَا، وَيُشِيرُ إلَى صَدْرِهِ ثَلَاثَ مَرَّاتٍ، بِحَسْبِ امْرِئٍ مِنْ الشَّرِّ أَنْ يَحْقِرَ أَخَاهُ الْمُسْلِمَ، كُلُّ الْمُسْلِمِ عَلَى الْمُسْلِمِ حَرَامٌ: دَمُهُ وَمَالُهُ وَعِرْضُهُ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not envy one another, do not inflate prices against one another, do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and do not undercut one another’s sales. Be, O servants of Allah, brothers. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim: he does not wrong him, abandon him, lie to him or look down on him. Taqwā is here,” and he pointed to his chest three times. “It is enough evil for a person to look down on his Muslim brother. All of a Muslim is sacred to another Muslim: his blood, his wealth and his honour.”", "lessons": ["Envy, hatred and cutting off people destroy brotherhood.", "Fair trade is part of brotherhood: no price-rigging or undercutting.", "Taqwā is in the heart, so do not judge people by appearance.", "Looking down on a Muslim is a great evil in itself."], "quiz": [["Which of these is forbidden in this ḥadīth?", "Envying one another", "Greeting one another", "Helping one another", "Visiting one another"], ["Where did the Prophet ﷺ point when he said “Taqwā is here”?", "His chest", "His head", "His tongue", "The sky"], ["How many times did he point?", "Three times", "Once", "Twice", "Seven times"], ["What is “enough evil” for a person?", "Looking down on his Muslim brother", "Missing a voluntary fast on Monday", "Eating a little more than he needs", "Sleeping early after the ʿIshāʾ prayer"], ["What three things of a Muslim are sacred to another Muslim?", "Blood, wealth and honour", "House, land and animals", "Name, tribe and city", "Time, health and youth"]]},
  {"n": 36, "title": "Relieving others and seeking knowledge", "narrator": "Abū Hurayrah", "source": "Muslim (2699)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ عَنْ النَّبِيِّ ﷺ قَالَ: مَنْ نَفَّسَ عَنْ مُؤْمِنٍ كُرْبَةً مِنْ كُرَبِ الدُّنْيَا نَفَّسَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ كُرْبَةً مِنْ كُرَبِ يَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ، وَمَنْ يَسَّرَ عَلَى مُعْسِرٍ، يَسَّرَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ، وَمَنْ سَتَرَ مُسْلِمًا سَتَرَهُ اللَّهُ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ، وَاَللَّهُ فِي عَوْنِ الْعَبْدِ مَا كَانَ الْعَبْدُ فِي عَوْنِ أَخِيهِ، وَمَنْ سَلَكَ طَرِيقًا يَلْتَمِسُ فِيهِ عِلْمًا سَهَّلَ اللَّهُ لَهُ بِهِ طَرِيقًا إلَى الْجَنَّةِ، وَمَا اجْتَمَعَ قَوْمٌ فِي بَيْتٍ مِنْ بُيُوتِ اللَّهِ يَتْلُونَ كِتَابَ اللَّهِ، وَيَتَدَارَسُونَهُ فِيمَا بَيْنَهُمْ؛ إلَّا نَزَلَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ السَّكِينَةُ، وَغَشِيَتْهُمْ الرَّحْمَةُ، وَحَفَّتْهُمُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ، وَذَكَرَهُمْ اللَّهُ فِيمَنْ عِنْدَهُ، وَمَنْ بَطَّأَ بِهِ عَمَلُهُ لَمْ يُسْرِعْ بِهِ نَسَبُهُ", "en": "The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever relieves a believer of a hardship of this world, Allah will relieve him of a hardship of the Day of Resurrection. Whoever makes things easy for someone in difficulty, Allah will make things easy for him in this world and the Hereafter. Whoever covers a Muslim’s faults, Allah will cover his faults in this world and the Hereafter. Allah is in the help of His servant as long as the servant is in the help of his brother. Whoever takes a path seeking knowledge, Allah makes easy for him a path to Paradise. No people gather in one of the houses of Allah, reciting the Book of Allah and studying it among themselves, except that tranquillity descends on them, mercy covers them, the angels surround them and Allah mentions them among those with Him. And whoever is slowed down by his deeds will not be hastened by his lineage.”", "lessons": ["Your reward matches your deed: help others, and Allah helps you.", "Covering others’ faults earns Allah’s covering of yours.", "Seeking knowledge is a path to Paradise, and study circles of the Qur’an are blessed.", "Family and lineage cannot replace good deeds."], "quiz": [["Whoever relieves a believer of a worldly hardship, Allah will:", "Relieve him of a hardship on the Day of Resurrection", "Make him wealthy in this world straight away", "Make him famous and respected among the people", "Give him a long and healthy life in this world"], ["Allah is in the help of His servant as long as:", "The servant helps his brother", "The servant becomes wealthy", "The servant becomes a scholar", "The servant stays in the mosque"], ["What does Allah make easy for whoever takes a path seeking knowledge?", "A path to Paradise", "A path to wealth", "A path to leadership", "A path to fame"], ["Which of these is NOT mentioned for people studying the Qur’an together?", "They become rich", "Tranquillity descends on them", "The angels surround them", "Allah mentions them"], ["“Whoever is slowed down by his deeds will not be hastened by his…”", "Lineage", "Wealth", "Knowledge", "Friends"]]},
  {"n": 37, "title": "How good and bad deeds are recorded", "narrator": "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (6491) and Muslim (131)", "ar": "عَنْ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ﷺ فِيمَا يَرْوِيهِ عَنْ رَبِّهِ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى، قَالَ: إنَّ اللَّهَ كَتَبَ الْحَسَنَاتِ وَالسَّيِّئَاتِ، ثُمَّ بَيَّنَ ذَلِكَ، فَمَنْ هَمَّ بِحَسَنَةٍ فَلَمْ يَعْمَلْهَا كَتَبَهَا اللَّهُ عِنْدَهُ حَسَنَةً كَامِلَةً، وَإِنْ هَمَّ بِهَا فَعَمِلَهَا كَتَبَهَا اللَّهُ عِنْدَهُ عَشْرَ حَسَنَاتٍ إلَى سَبْعِمِائَةِ ضِعْفٍ إلَى أَضْعَافٍ كَثِيرَةٍ، وَإِنْ هَمَّ بِسَيِّئَةٍ فَلَمْ يَعْمَلْهَا كَتَبَهَا اللَّهُ عِنْدَهُ حَسَنَةً كَامِلَةً، وَإِنْ هَمَّ بِهَا فَعَمِلَهَا كَتَبَهَا اللَّهُ سَيِّئَةً وَاحِدَةً.،، في صحيحيهما بهذه الحروف", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrating from his Lord, said: “Allah has written good deeds and bad deeds, then made that clear. Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, Allah writes it with Him as a complete good deed. If he intends it and does it, Allah writes it with Him as ten good deeds, up to seven hundred times, up to many times more. Whoever intends a bad deed and does not do it, Allah writes it with Him as a complete good deed. If he intends it and does it, Allah writes it as one bad deed.”", "lessons": ["Allah’s generosity: a good intention alone is rewarded.", "Good deeds are multiplied ten to seven hundred times and more.", "Leaving a sin for Allah’s sake is rewarded as a good deed.", "A bad deed done is written as only one; never despair of Allah’s mercy."], "quiz": [["Someone intends a good deed but does not do it. What is written?", "One complete good deed", "Nothing at all", "One bad deed", "Ten good deeds"], ["A good deed that is done is written as at least:", "Ten good deeds", "One good deed", "Two good deeds", "Five good deeds"], ["Someone intends a bad deed but leaves it. What is written?", "A complete good deed", "A bad deed", "Half a bad deed", "Nothing"], ["A bad deed that is done is written as:", "One bad deed", "Ten bad deeds", "Seven hundred bad deeds", "Two bad deeds"], ["This ḥadīth mainly shows:", "Allah’s generosity and mercy", "How to count prayers", "The rules of trade", "The signs of the Hour"]]},
  {"n": 38, "title": "The friends of Allah", "narrator": "Abū Hurayrah", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (6502)", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَة رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُول اللَّهِ ﷺ إنَّ اللَّهَ تَعَالَى قَالَ: مَنْ عَادَى لِي وَلِيًّا فَقَدْ آذَنْتهُ بِالْحَرْبِ، وَمَا تَقَرَّبَ إلَيَّ عَبْدِي بِشَيْءٍ أَحَبَّ إلَيَّ مِمَّا افْتَرَضْتُهُ عَلَيْهِ، وَلَا يَزَالُ عَبْدِي يَتَقَرَّبُ إلَيَّ بِالنَّوَافِلِ حَتَّى أُحِبَّهُ، فَإِذَا أَحْبَبْتُهُ كُنْت سَمْعَهُ الَّذِي يَسْمَعُ بِهِ، وَبَصَرَهُ الَّذِي يُبْصِرُ بِهِ، وَيَدَهُ الَّتِي يَبْطِشُ بِهَا، وَرِجْلَهُ الَّتِي يَمْشِي بِهَا، وَلَئِنْ سَأَلَنِي لَأُعْطِيَنَّهُ، وَلَئِنْ اسْتَعَاذَنِي لَأُعِيذَنَّهُ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah the Exalted said: Whoever shows enmity to a friend of Mine, I have declared war on him. My servant does not draw near to Me with anything more beloved to Me than what I have made obligatory on him. And My servant keeps drawing near to Me with voluntary deeds until I love him. When I love him, I become his hearing with which he hears, his sight with which he sees, his hand with which he strikes and his foot with which he walks. If he asks Me, I will surely give him, and if he seeks refuge with Me, I will surely protect him.”", "lessons": ["The friends of Allah (awliyāʾ) are the believers who fear Him; harming them is very serious.", "Obligations are the most beloved way to draw near to Allah; start there.", "Voluntary deeds after the obligations bring Allah’s love.", "Allah guides the hearing, sight and actions of the one He loves, and answers his duʿāʾ."], "quiz": [["What does Allah declare against whoever shows enmity to His friend?", "War", "Peace", "Pardon", "Delay"], ["What is the most beloved way to draw near to Allah?", "The obligations", "Voluntary fasts", "Travelling", "Building mosques"], ["The servant keeps drawing near with voluntary deeds until:", "Allah loves him", "He becomes rich", "He stops sinning forever", "People praise him"], ["“I become his hearing with which he hears” means:", "Allah guides his hearing to what pleases Him", "He is able to hear everything in the world", "He becomes free of every human weakness", "He no longer needs to listen to anyone"], ["What kind of ḥadīth is this?", "A ḥadīth qudsī", "A ḥadīth mursal", "A weak ḥadīth", "A Companion’s saying"]]},
  {"n": 39, "title": "Mistakes, forgetfulness and coercion", "narrator": "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās", "source": "Ibn Mājah (2045) and al-Bayhaqī; graded ḥasan by an-Nawawī", "ar": "عَنْ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ قَالَ: إنَّ اللَّهَ تَجَاوَزَ لِي عَنْ أُمَّتِي الْخَطَأَ وَالنِّسْيَانَ وَمَا اسْتُكْرِهُوا عَلَيْهِ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has pardoned my nation for me their mistakes, their forgetfulness and what they are forced to do.”", "lessons": ["A person is not sinful for genuine mistakes, forgetfulness or real coercion.", "This shows the ease of the Sharīʿah and Allah’s mercy to this nation.", "Some worldly consequences may remain, such as repaying damaged property or making up a missed prayer.", "It matches the duʿāʾ at the end of al-Baqarah: “Our Lord, do not take us to task if we forget or err.”"], "quiz": [["How many things has Allah pardoned in this ḥadīth?", "Three", "Two", "Four", "Five"], ["Which of these is pardoned?", "Forgetfulness", "Deliberate sin", "Laziness", "Delaying repentance"], ["If someone forgets a prayer, what remains?", "He prays it when he remembers", "Nothing at all", "He must fast instead", "He must give charity instead"], ["This ḥadīth shows that the Sharīʿah is built on:", "Ease and mercy", "Hardship and blame", "Punishment for all errors", "Strict penalties only"], ["Which verse matches this ḥadīth?", "The end of Sūrat al-Baqarah", "The start of Sūrat al-Fātiḥah", "Āyat al-Kursī", "Sūrat al-Ikhlāṣ"]]},
  {"n": 40, "title": "Be in this world like a stranger", "narrator": "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar", "source": "Al-Bukhārī (6416)", "ar": "عَنْ ابْن عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: أَخَذَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ بِمَنْكِبِي، وَقَالَ: كُنْ فِي الدُّنْيَا كَأَنَّك غَرِيبٌ أَوْ عَابِرُ سَبِيلٍ. وَكَانَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا يَقُولُ: إذَا أَمْسَيْتَ فَلَا تَنْتَظِرْ الصَّبَاحَ، وَإِذَا أَصْبَحْتَ فَلَا تَنْتَظِرْ الْمَسَاءَ، وَخُذْ مِنْ صِحَّتِك لِمَرَضِك، وَمِنْ حَيَاتِك لِمَوْتِك", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of my shoulder and said: “Be in this world as though you were a stranger or a traveller passing through.” And Ibn ʿUmar used to say: “When evening comes, do not wait for the morning; and when morning comes, do not wait for the evening. Take from your health for your sickness, and from your life for your death.”", "lessons": ["A stranger does not settle or compete for status; a traveller only takes what he needs for the journey.", "The Prophet ﷺ taught with touch and closeness: he held Ibn ʿUmar’s shoulder.", "Do good now; do not delay to a tomorrow that may not come.", "Use health, youth and time while you have them."], "quiz": [["How did the Prophet ﷺ get Ibn ʿUmar’s attention?", "He took hold of his shoulder", "He called him loudly", "He wrote him a letter", "He sent a messenger"], ["We should be in this world like:", "A stranger or a traveller passing through", "A king who lives in his palace for ever", "A merchant who never leaves his shop", "A guard who stands always at the gate"], ["Ibn ʿUmar said: when evening comes, do not wait for:", "The morning", "The night", "The next week", "The next year"], ["“Take from your health for your sickness” means:", "Do good deeds while you are healthy", "Save your medicine for a later time", "Avoid all exercise to keep strength", "Eat less food so you will not fall ill"], ["Which collection recorded this ḥadīth?", "Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī", "Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim", "Sunan at-Tirmidhī", "Sunan an-Nasāʾī"]]},
  {"n": 41, "title": "Desires that follow the Revelation", "narrator": "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ", "source": "An-Nawawī said: ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ, narrated in Kitāb al-Ḥujjah. Several later scholars, such as Ibn Rajab, judged its chain weak; its meaning is supported by the Qur’an (an-Nisāʾ 4:65).", "ar": "عَنْ أَبِي مُحَمَّدٍ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَمْرِو بْنِ الْعَاصِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ لَا يُؤْمِنُ أَحَدُكُمْ حَتَّى يَكُونَ هَوَاهُ تَبَعًا لِمَا جِئْتُ بِهِ", "en": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you truly believes until his desires follow what I have brought.”", "lessons": ["Complete faith means bringing your wishes in line with the Qur’an and Sunnah.", "A believer does not pick only the rulings he likes.", "Its meaning is confirmed by the Qur’an: “No, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what they dispute” (an-Nisāʾ 4:65).", "Students should know how scholars graded a ḥadīth: an-Nawawī authenticated it, while others weakened its chain."], "quiz": [["Complete faith requires that a person’s desires:", "Follow what the Prophet ﷺ brought", "Are always fulfilled", "Are completely removed", "Follow the customs of his people"], ["Which verse supports the meaning of this ḥadīth?", "An-Nisāʾ 4:65", "Al-Fātiḥah 1:1", "Al-Ikhlāṣ 112:1", "An-Nās 114:1"], ["An-Nawawī graded this ḥadīth:", "Ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ", "Fabricated", "Mursal", "Very weak"], ["Ibn Rajab and others judged its chain:", "Weak", "Mutawātir", "Ṣaḥīḥ", "Mawḍūʿ"], ["Who narrated this ḥadīth?", "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ", "ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ ibn Wāʾil", "ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib", "ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd al-Hudhalī"]]},
  {"n": 42, "title": "The vastness of Allah’s forgiveness", "narrator": "Anas ibn Mālik", "source": "At-Tirmidhī (3540), who said: ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ", "ar": "عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: سَمِعْت رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ يَقُولُ: قَالَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: يَا ابْنَ آدَمَ! إِنَّكَ مَا دَعَوْتنِي وَرَجَوْتنِي غَفَرْتُ لَك عَلَى مَا كَانَ مِنْك وَلَا أُبَالِي، يَا ابْنَ آدَمَ! لَوْ بَلَغَتْ ذُنُوبُك عَنَانَ السَّمَاءِ ثُمَّ اسْتَغْفَرْتنِي غَفَرْتُ لَك، يَا ابْنَ آدَمَ! إنَّك لَوْ أَتَيْتنِي بِقُرَابِ الْأَرْضِ خَطَايَا ثُمَّ لَقِيتنِي لَا تُشْرِكُ بِي شَيْئًا لَأَتَيْتُك بِقُرَابِهَا مَغْفِرَةً", "en": "I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah the Exalted said: O son of Ādam, as long as you call on Me and hope in Me, I will forgive you for what you have done, and I do not mind. O son of Ādam, if your sins reached the clouds of the sky and then you asked Me for forgiveness, I would forgive you. O son of Ādam, if you came to Me with sins nearly filling the earth and then met Me not associating anything with Me, I would come to you with forgiveness nearly filling it.”", "lessons": ["Three keys to forgiveness: duʿāʾ with hope, seeking forgiveness (istighfār), and tawḥīd.", "No sin is too big for Allah’s forgiveness when a person turns back to Him.", "Shirk is the one sin that blocks this forgiveness if a person dies on it.", "The Arbaʿīn ends with hope: never despair of the mercy of Allah."], "quiz": [["What kind of ḥadīth is this?", "A ḥadīth qudsī", "A ḥadīth mursal", "A Companion’s saying", "A weak ḥadīth"], ["If your sins reached the clouds of the sky and you sought forgiveness, Allah would:", "Forgive you", "Forgive half of them", "Delay His answer", "Ask for more deeds"], ["What condition is mentioned with sins nearly filling the earth?", "Meeting Allah without associating partners with Him", "Giving all your wealth in charity before you die", "Fasting every single day for a whole year", "Praying in the Masjid al-Ḥarām in Makkah"], ["Which of these is NOT one of the keys to forgiveness in this ḥadīth?", "Being from a noble family", "Calling on Allah with hope", "Seeking forgiveness", "Tawḥīd"], ["The Arbaʿīn ends with a message of:", "Hope in Allah’s mercy", "Fear of punishment only", "The signs of the Hour", "The rules of trade"]]}
];
